00:28:59.260 --> 00:28:59.820
Love

00:29:00.000 --> 00:29:00.860
Return

00:29:01.360 --> 00:29:02.850
In a

00:29:04.500 --> 00:29:04.740
Head

00:31:14.880 --> 00:31:20.870
Gee, what a dump. Are we really gonna stay here?

00:31:21.200 --> 00:31:22.940
Hey, you made this mess!

00:31:23.800 --> 00:31:26.120
Oh my! I didn't know you cared!

00:31:26.780 --> 00:31:27.140
Sweet.

00:31:28.630 --> 00:31:29.150
Welcome!

00:31:30.000 --> 00:31:32.100
It's a long trip. Thanks for coming all the way.

00:31:32.460 --> 00:31:35.120
Well, thank you for inviting us back again.

00:31:37.200 --> 00:31:38.160
Here you go.

00:31:42.510 --> 00:31:44.810
Boys, you get to work repairing the damage.

00:31:45.210 --> 00:31:47.750
Girls, you start on cleaning, laundry, and cooking.

00:31:50.650 --> 00:31:54.110
But we're tired. Can't we rest a little bit first?

00:31:54.870 --> 00:31:55.630
What did you say?

00:31:55.770 --> 00:31:57.570
Me? Oh, nothing.

00:31:58.110 --> 00:31:59.930
We should probably do what she said.

00:32:00.570 --> 00:32:03.230
That's right. Come on, let's go now.

00:32:04.150 --> 00:32:07.050
Excuse me, ma'am, pardon me. What's my assignment to be?

00:32:07.270 --> 00:32:08.690
You're new, aren't you?

00:32:09.440 --> 00:32:15.980
Yes, I am. How do you do? My name is Washu, and I am at your service, oh great, respected one.

00:32:17.010 --> 00:32:22.470
Well, well, for being so young and all, you are a good, polite girl, and I like that.

00:32:23.020 --> 00:32:28.840
Now, I'm not planning on making any children do any work, so why don't you run along with Sasami and play?

00:32:30.920 --> 00:32:31.560
Yes, ma'am.

00:32:31.720 --> 00:32:32.080
Hm?

00:32:34.240 --> 00:32:34.500
Huh?

00:32:37.320 --> 00:32:38.560
Washu, you slacker!

00:32:39.980 --> 00:32:40.240
Ouch!

00:32:40.990 --> 00:32:42.390
Just what the-

00:32:42.480 --> 00:32:44.740
Quit wasting my time.

00:32:51.880 --> 00:32:54.000
Boo-yuki.

00:32:54.260 --> 00:32:58.060
I thought you were a party of eight, but it looks like we got one more guest.

00:32:58.220 --> 00:32:58.460
Huh?

00:32:59.010 --> 00:32:59.310
Eh?

00:33:01.660 --> 00:33:05.530
What are you talking about? There are only eight of us.

00:33:09.800 --> 00:33:14.690
Strange. I could swear I saw a young lady resembling me as a young woman.

00:33:15.500 --> 00:33:18.480
Well, there's no one like that with us. Not at all.

00:33:18.800 --> 00:33:20.660
She's starting to see things.

00:33:22.140 --> 00:33:22.740
Watch out.

00:33:23.380 --> 00:33:25.940
I said get to work and I mean it.

00:33:26.140 --> 00:33:27.320
Yes, ma'am.

00:33:28.020 --> 00:33:28.700
Shall we go?

00:33:29.490 --> 00:33:29.830
Okay.

00:33:34.380 --> 00:33:35.500
Hey, Ayeka!

00:33:36.750 --> 00:33:36.930
Hmm?

00:33:37.880 --> 00:33:39.360
Uh, nothing.

00:33:39.780 --> 00:33:40.600
Never mind.

00:33:43.650 --> 00:33:45.120
Come on now, Sasami.

00:33:46.790 --> 00:33:47.050
Okay.

00:34:02.620 --> 00:34:03.820
This is a milfoil.

00:34:04.400 --> 00:34:09.060
Did you know these flowers are supposedly grown for their beauty and medicinal values?

00:34:09.300 --> 00:34:10.740
But I wonder what they cure.

00:34:13.320 --> 00:34:13.840
Sasami!

00:34:14.080 --> 00:34:15.800
Come over here, Sasami!

00:34:16.040 --> 00:34:17.620
Come on, it's a wonderful view.

00:34:17.620 --> 00:34:18.740
It really is.

00:34:30.640 --> 00:34:31.280
Sasami!

00:34:31.710 --> 00:34:37.530
What? Where'd she go?

00:34:38.720 --> 00:34:42.830
Oh, well, Ryo-Oki is with her, so she'll be fine, I'm sure.

00:34:44.330 --> 00:34:51.470
This must be what she had in mind when she called and invited us over.

00:34:52.380 --> 00:34:54.960
Hmm, I was so stupid.

00:34:55.750 --> 00:34:57.230
Let's just say naive.

00:34:57.940 --> 00:34:59.980
Well, you were excited about coming here, too.

00:35:00.000 --> 00:35:01.700
Did you say something?

00:35:02.160 --> 00:35:04.000
No, nothing, nothing.

00:35:08.320 --> 00:35:10.280
I told you to be careful.

00:35:17.040 --> 00:35:18.950
Hey, Tenchi, look!

00:35:21.030 --> 00:35:22.800
Now who's a bonehead?

00:35:35.270 --> 00:35:37.570
You're a big help with the way you're peeling them.

00:35:37.670 --> 00:35:39.070
We won't have anything left to eat.

00:35:40.150 --> 00:35:41.010
Is that right?

00:35:41.290 --> 00:35:43.030
Well, with how slowly you're peeling them,

00:35:43.150 --> 00:35:45.150
we're never going to finish, Madam Slowpoke.

00:35:46.850 --> 00:35:49.530
Well, at least I have a talent for not wasting food.

00:35:50.360 --> 00:35:51.220
What are you saying?

00:35:51.500 --> 00:35:52.160
The truth.

00:35:53.840 --> 00:35:55.680
Settle down, both of you.

00:35:55.780 --> 00:35:58.320
I mean, let's not argue over nothing, okay?

00:35:58.540 --> 00:35:59.980
I mean, at least wait till it's...

00:36:00.030 --> 00:36:01.570
Something to argue about

00:36:15.060 --> 00:36:27.700
Do anything tell you I really didn't do anything and you better believe me

00:36:30.250 --> 00:36:30.810
Was it you?

00:36:32.880 --> 00:36:33.720
Oh, Aika.

00:36:34.690 --> 00:36:34.930
Hm?

00:36:36.360 --> 00:36:39.080
Did you see someone else here just now?

00:36:40.000 --> 00:36:41.480
No, Aika, I didn't.

00:36:42.010 --> 00:36:42.330
Meow.

00:36:43.140 --> 00:36:44.500
I thought I saw someone.

00:36:45.340 --> 00:36:47.140
Aika, I need to tell you-

00:36:47.140 --> 00:36:48.760
Hey, Aika, what was it?

00:36:49.060 --> 00:36:49.640
Oh, nothing!

00:36:50.800 --> 00:36:53.220
Uh, Sasami, you were saying?

00:36:53.870 --> 00:36:55.170
Uh, nothing, really.

00:36:57.760 --> 00:36:57.960
Hm?

00:36:58.850 --> 00:36:59.050
Hm.

00:37:02.040 --> 00:37:03.620
Please, hold it tight, Grandpa.

00:37:03.960 --> 00:37:05.440
I know. Hurry up.

00:37:10.360 --> 00:37:17.930
Did you see that?

00:37:24.750 --> 00:37:29.350
I was telling you what we saw.

00:37:30.000 --> 00:37:32.240
A vague, ghost-like figure.

00:37:32.880 --> 00:37:36.520
Oh, okay, you guys are just trying to scare me now, right?

00:37:37.200 --> 00:37:39.080
No, we actually saw it.

00:37:39.920 --> 00:37:42.430
You saw it?

00:37:42.860 --> 00:37:43.340
Yes.

00:37:44.240 --> 00:37:49.350
Come to think of it, Dad and Grandpa said they saw something, something similar.

00:37:50.290 --> 00:37:53.970
Stop it, please! I can't stand it! I can't stand it!

00:37:55.710 --> 00:37:57.370
What are you afraid of, Tenshi?

00:37:57.690 --> 00:37:59.310
Hey, do I look afraid?

00:38:01.780 --> 00:38:02.340
Grandpa!

00:38:03.910 --> 00:38:06.850
Listen, I'll tell you the story.

00:38:07.660 --> 00:38:10.860
When I was a young man, the person who lived here told it to me.

00:38:11.060 --> 00:38:13.380
It begins over 600 years ago.

00:38:14.060 --> 00:38:17.520
There was a house on a mountain, far away from civilization.

00:38:17.880 --> 00:38:19.140
In it there lived a couple.

00:38:19.500 --> 00:38:24.240
People respected and admired their relationship because they were so much in love.

00:38:24.650 --> 00:38:29.530
However, the wife had been sickly since childhood and had become bedridden for quite some time.

00:38:30.800 --> 00:38:34.220
It is said she probably knew that her time was running short.

00:38:34.500 --> 00:38:39.040
They did their best trying to care for each other and live their lives to the fullest

00:38:39.040 --> 00:38:41.840
and to treasure their remaining time together.

00:38:43.690 --> 00:38:47.530
One stormy night, they heard a voice through the howling wind.

00:38:47.850 --> 00:38:49.510
It wasn't their imagination.

00:38:49.900 --> 00:38:51.520
The voice was real.

00:38:52.460 --> 00:38:54.760
Though they were scared, they were compelled to listen,

00:38:54.780 --> 00:38:56.960
and this is what the voice said to them.

00:38:58.890 --> 00:38:59.950
Head to the west.

00:39:00.510 --> 00:39:05.410
Go over three mountains and you'll find an herb that can cure any kind of sickness.

00:39:06.830 --> 00:39:10.220
Thus the wind spoke and then fell silent.

00:39:11.020 --> 00:39:14.940
The husband believed the wind's words and decided to go search for the herb.

00:39:15.520 --> 00:39:21.000
She begged him to remain and not leave her alone, but he left and set out for the west.

00:39:24.380 --> 00:39:29.900
For six months, she waited for his return.

00:39:30.540 --> 00:39:35.050
holding on against death with all her strength, but he didn't return.

00:39:35.650 --> 00:39:37.330
She spoke to herself, saying,

00:39:37.830 --> 00:39:41.890
I wish that I were healthy, then I would be able to look for him.

00:39:42.230 --> 00:39:50.000
But, alas, her hopes were in vain, and one day, all alone, she passed away.

00:39:52.400 --> 00:39:56.720
After that day, around this place, people began to see an image of a woman.

00:39:56.820 --> 00:39:59.350
They call her the White Ghost.

00:40:00.320 --> 00:40:01.900
So you'd better watch out, Tenshi.

00:40:02.140 --> 00:40:02.300
Hmm?

00:40:03.560 --> 00:40:08.160
Her spirit wanders aimlessly, searching for her beloved, constantly searching.

00:40:08.500 --> 00:40:10.880
She may even come for you.

00:40:13.560 --> 00:40:13.860
Hey!

00:40:14.240 --> 00:40:14.560
Ah!

00:40:17.130 --> 00:40:18.590
Haven't you rested long enough?

00:40:18.980 --> 00:40:20.260
Get back to work!

00:40:22.650 --> 00:40:23.670
Yes, ma'am!

00:40:25.040 --> 00:40:25.840
Kids today!

00:40:27.040 --> 00:40:29.840
Hey, that goes for you, too, I hope you know.

00:40:30.250 --> 00:40:32.720
But, but I, the white ghost is...

00:40:33.290 --> 00:40:34.950
Not the white ghost!

00:40:36.110 --> 00:40:39.300
That old story of yours again?

00:40:39.990 --> 00:40:41.370
You, your story?

00:40:41.890 --> 00:40:43.650
That you made it all up?

00:40:46.100 --> 00:40:48.050
Yep, not mad, are you?

00:40:48.310 --> 00:40:49.270
Cut it out!

00:40:51.070 --> 00:40:52.710
Don't fix the lights or something.

00:40:57.010 --> 00:40:58.730
When will they ever grow up?

00:41:01.180 --> 00:41:11.670
Why am I the one who has to fix this dad and grandpa are always sitting around doing nothing, huh?

00:41:18.110 --> 00:41:23.650
So what if grandpa's story was all made up? I mean we all did see that white image

00:41:23.650 --> 00:41:29.710
Haha, I better stop thinking about ghosts or I'll probably see one

00:41:32.620 --> 00:41:49.250
Hey, it's only me. It's just a stupid can.

00:42:00.000 --> 00:42:01.780
Ha ha ha ha ha ha ha ha!

00:42:07.710 --> 00:42:08.790
Ah gah gah gah!

00:42:10.780 --> 00:42:11.300
Doooooah!

00:42:12.670 --> 00:42:12.970
Tchii!

00:42:30.090 --> 00:42:31.590
Now, where did he go?

00:42:34.710 --> 00:42:35.690
You've seen it?

00:42:36.330 --> 00:42:36.630
Yep.

00:42:37.910 --> 00:42:39.090
I'm scared!

00:42:39.490 --> 00:42:42.340
Hmm. I need to know something.

00:42:42.580 --> 00:42:44.200
Where did you see it exactly?

00:42:44.600 --> 00:42:45.780
Uh, you know.

00:42:48.820 --> 00:42:49.100
Huh?

00:42:50.630 --> 00:42:55.600
Hmm, my imagination.

00:43:00.320 --> 00:43:00.920
Sasami?

00:43:05.660 --> 00:43:06.420
Sasami?

00:43:06.720 --> 00:43:08.880
Not so tight!

00:43:10.740 --> 00:43:15.820
Well, Sasami, it's only you.

00:43:16.330 --> 00:43:17.600
I can't breathe.

00:43:20.750 --> 00:43:24.240
My, that was so scary.

00:43:24.240 --> 00:43:25.900
I thought it was...

00:43:26.410 --> 00:43:26.770
Huh?

00:43:30.000 --> 00:43:31.120
REFLECTION IS!

00:43:36.110 --> 00:43:36.790
Tsunami?

00:43:43.120 --> 00:43:43.640
Tsunami!

00:44:05.850 --> 00:44:06.890
She's not around here anywhere.

00:44:07.130 --> 00:44:07.370
I look.

00:44:07.550 --> 00:44:08.730
She's not inside the inn.

00:44:09.270 --> 00:44:09.750
Washu?

00:44:10.160 --> 00:44:10.640
Nope.

00:44:12.630 --> 00:44:13.110
I've checked.

00:44:13.590 --> 00:44:15.630
My instruments can't seem to find a trace of her.

00:44:16.220 --> 00:44:19.280
I can't communicate with Rio Oki now, either.

00:44:20.410 --> 00:44:23.450
We'll just have to spread out and search for her ourselves.

00:44:23.830 --> 00:44:25.290
Well, I'll go this way.

00:44:25.510 --> 00:44:25.910
All right.

00:44:29.370 --> 00:44:29.650
Huh.

00:44:30.090 --> 00:44:33.010
Let's see. I'll go this way, then...

00:44:33.010 --> 00:44:36.490
You! Go that way!

00:44:38.390 --> 00:44:43.250
Sasami! Sasami! Sasami, where are you?

00:44:45.140 --> 00:44:53.180
Are you? That reflection was of Tsunami. Then what is happening to Sasami?

00:45:03.000 --> 00:45:29.970
Thank you for watching!

00:45:30.220 --> 00:45:51.490
alone. Oh, okay. Sorry, Aika, but I'm not the real Sasami. Huh? What do you mean, Sasami?

00:46:01.880 --> 00:46:02.440
Sasami.

00:46:02.950 --> 00:46:03.350
Oh.

00:46:10.110 --> 00:46:11.470
700 years ago.

00:46:12.590 --> 00:46:15.550
Yes, it all happened 700 years ago.

00:46:18.590 --> 00:46:22.590
That day when the space pirate Ryoko attacked planet Jirai.

00:46:24.030 --> 00:46:25.230
Intruder in block 194.

00:46:25.590 --> 00:46:26.990
Intruder in block 194.

00:46:27.350 --> 00:46:29.960
Princess Sasami, where are you?

00:46:30.890 --> 00:46:40.240
Sasami! Sasami!

00:46:52.230 --> 00:46:54.880
Sasami, where could she have gone?

00:46:56.560 --> 00:46:57.440
Where did she go?

00:46:58.220 --> 00:46:58.740
Wow!

00:47:01.630 --> 00:47:04.370
WHAA-

00:47:05.260 --> 00:47:05.980
NAAA

00:48:56.080 --> 00:48:56.300
Mama!

00:48:57.620 --> 00:48:58.560
Mrs. Sasami!

00:49:00.890 --> 00:49:02.890
Is my little princess all right?

00:49:03.150 --> 00:49:03.590
Yes.

00:49:04.260 --> 00:49:04.820
Oh, good.

00:49:11.330 --> 00:49:13.940
Trash, I hate to tell you many times.

00:49:15.290 --> 00:49:17.290
The real sister Sammy died that day.

00:49:17.990 --> 00:49:22.510
Therefore, I am... I am not your real sister.

00:49:35.240 --> 00:49:36.940
Nika, please wait!

00:50:00.000 --> 00:50:00.580
Sasami?

00:50:04.870 --> 00:50:06.250
I'm sorry, Sasami.

00:50:09.860 --> 00:50:18.120
Telling me this, Sasami?

00:50:19.540 --> 00:50:22.960
Um, are you telling me this to drive me away?

00:50:29.580 --> 00:50:29.980
You...

00:50:30.350 --> 00:50:33.070
I do! I really...

00:50:33.160 --> 00:50:34.040
Really?

00:50:34.850 --> 00:50:36.590
Yes, I do! Yes, I do!

00:50:37.190 --> 00:50:40.510
You do? I love you too, Sasami.

00:50:43.490 --> 00:50:45.940
We love each other. That's what counts.

00:50:51.540 --> 00:50:52.140
Tenchi?

00:50:53.740 --> 00:50:55.010
Uh, I...

00:50:56.640 --> 00:50:57.240
I...

00:51:00.510 --> 00:51:02.030
Feel the same as Aieka.

00:51:03.970 --> 00:51:06.530
Sasami, we like you just the way you are.

00:51:07.570 --> 00:51:08.780
Right, Sasami.

00:51:09.440 --> 00:51:11.780
Whatever happens, you are my dear sister.

00:51:12.990 --> 00:51:13.550
Aieka.

00:51:14.260 --> 00:51:25.760
That's fine.

00:51:28.420 --> 00:51:29.980
Sasami is a little girl after.

00:51:30.000 --> 00:51:31.460
After all, let's see.

00:51:31.680 --> 00:51:43.150
Looks like she's fallen asleep.

00:51:43.840 --> 00:51:45.300
Yes, it looks that way.

00:51:46.320 --> 00:51:47.660
The poor dear is exhausted.

00:51:48.020 --> 00:51:51.930
I guess she was afraid after we found out about her secret, we would leave her.

00:51:53.340 --> 00:51:56.210
She told me that the real Sasami died.

00:51:56.430 --> 00:51:59.850
But if that's true, then up, Princess Aika.

00:52:09.920 --> 00:52:12.140
Sami didn't really die, Princess Aika.

00:52:13.160 --> 00:52:16.160
She thinks of herself as my creation,

00:52:16.820 --> 00:52:19.440
but she actually survived by assimilating with me.

00:52:20.120 --> 00:52:21.020
She's still young.

00:52:21.380 --> 00:52:23.180
One day she will understand everything.

00:52:25.120 --> 00:52:26.140
I don't understand.

00:52:26.140 --> 00:52:27.440
Why didn't you tell her?

00:52:28.380 --> 00:52:29.980
She wouldn't have believed it, Princess Aika.

00:52:30.000 --> 00:52:31.980
Even if I had told her.

00:52:33.940 --> 00:52:37.370
Besides, Sasami needed to know of your feelings for her.

00:52:37.940 --> 00:52:40.840
Right now, that's more important than the truth of her identity.

00:52:41.630 --> 00:52:44.990
Princess Ayaka, she truly is your real sister.

00:53:07.450 --> 00:53:08.310
Here you are.

00:53:08.450 --> 00:53:09.630
We've been looking for you.

00:53:22.600 --> 00:53:28.080
Hey, come on, Tenshi.

00:53:28.240 --> 00:53:29.900
Come on, have a little suck.

00:53:30.840 --> 00:53:32.340
I'm still a minor.

00:53:32.810 --> 00:53:33.750
Go right ahead!

00:53:36.680 --> 00:53:38.080
Let's liven things up.

00:53:38.630 --> 00:53:39.130
What do you say?

00:53:42.670 --> 00:53:43.230
What?

00:54:00.250 --> 00:54:28.140
someone feeling kind of blue around here you know i didn't know that your eye had trees that could take on human form meaning tsunami and sesame are the same there get it so what

00:54:30.000 --> 00:54:37.780
No, they are assimilated. That means that Sasami and Tsunami are identical, which means that when Sasami grows up...

00:54:38.380 --> 00:54:42.100
She'll look like Tsunami? Hmm, can't be.

00:54:42.730 --> 00:54:59.390
Yes, she will be like me. We have separate minds right now, but when we are joined in one form, you can call me Sasami or Tsunami.

00:55:00.000 --> 00:55:01.040
Whichever one you prefer.

00:55:04.080 --> 00:55:04.400
Huh?

00:55:05.700 --> 00:55:06.740
You needn't worry.

00:55:08.500 --> 00:55:11.400
When we are united, she will have a complete memory.

00:55:12.010 --> 00:55:13.670
That's not why we're worried!

00:55:14.100 --> 00:55:14.380
Huh?

00:55:15.660 --> 00:55:17.680
So Sasami will look like you?

00:55:18.120 --> 00:55:21.000
Yes, I am the image of Sasami in the future.

00:55:22.210 --> 00:55:24.020
Damn, I didn't think about this.

00:55:24.300 --> 00:55:28.140
Since Ayaka's no competition, I thought Sasami was nothing to worry about.

00:55:28.910 --> 00:55:29.970
I didn't plan on that.

00:55:30.160 --> 00:55:32.700
This Asami's beauty will surpass mine.

00:55:34.600 --> 00:55:37.430
Well, she's a lot prettier than you are.

00:55:37.670 --> 00:55:41.040
And at least she's better looking than you are.

00:55:42.550 --> 00:55:43.410
What'd you say?

00:55:43.630 --> 00:55:45.010
I'm simply stating a fact.

00:55:45.770 --> 00:55:46.770
Shut up!

00:55:47.010 --> 00:55:48.330
Yeah, you stay out of this.

00:55:51.740 --> 00:55:54.100
Never were as pretty as me, ever. You never were.

00:55:54.350 --> 00:55:58.350
What? You just try and name one advantage you have over me.

00:55:58.830 --> 00:55:59.310
Everything.

00:56:00.730 --> 00:56:02.490
Well, well, don't argue like tha-

00:56:02.490 --> 00:56:03.330
AHHHHH!

00:56:03.970 --> 00:56:04.410
WAAAHHHHH!

00:56:19.000 --> 00:56:19.900
Are you two okay?

00:56:24.000 --> 00:56:25.200
Of course we aren't.

00:56:25.980 --> 00:56:28.140
What do you think, you simpleton?

00:56:28.570 --> 00:56:29.910
Oh, I-I'm so so-

00:56:30.000 --> 00:56:32.200
I'm gonna get you

00:57:01.080 --> 00:57:25.490
So graceful, so close, somehow, times I could find a way

00:57:30.250 --> 00:57:35.110
I whisper to the star in the sky

00:57:35.110 --> 00:57:43.980
So kiss in the sun

00:57:45.700 --> 00:57:50.560
I seem to count the hour

00:57:51.290 --> 00:57:53.780
When we are not together

00:57:53.780 --> 00:57:57.640
I've seen a tender fire in your eye

00:57:58.400 --> 00:57:59.980
Yet when I'm gone

00:58:00.570 --> 00:58:02.680
You carry on

00:58:05.870 --> 00:58:11.210
Antinetic love returns

00:58:11.390 --> 00:58:16.260
With the nut and the roll

01:00:00.000 --> 01:00:00.160
You
